DevOps Interview Experience – Key Questions & Answers

Today I faced an interview for a DevOps role, and here are some important questions along with simple explanations 👇

✅ 1. How do you take code from Git and deploy to Kubernetes using GitHub Actions?

Code is stored in GitHub
Create a workflow using GitHub Actions

Steps:
Trigger on push (CI/CD pipeline starts)
Build Docker image
Push image to registry (like Docker Hub / ECR)
Use kubectl to deploy to Kubernetes
Example tools used: Docker, kubectl, secrets for authentication

✅ 2. Difference between Jenkins and GitHub Actions

Jenkins
Manual setup required
High (plugins, servers)
Highly customizable
Works with many tools
Needs infra

GitHub Actions
Built-in with GitHub
Low (managed)
Easy but slightly limited
Best with GitHub repos
Free tier available

✅ 3. What is Kubernetes CrashLoopBackOff?

A state where a pod keeps failing and restarting

Common reasons:

 Application crash
 Wrong configuration
 Missing environment variables
Kubernetes waits before restarting again (backoff mechanism)

✅ 4. Why is Kubernetes important?

Automates deployment and scaling
Handles container orchestration
Provides high availability & self-healing
Works across cloud providers

✅ 5. Different types of scaling in Kubernetes

Horizontal Pod Autoscaler (HPA) → Adds/removes pods
Vertical Pod Autoscaler (VPA) → Adjusts CPU/memory
Cluster Autoscaler → Adds/removes nodes

✅ 6. What is the use of CloudWatch?

Amazon CloudWatch is used for:
Monitoring logs and metrics
Setting alarms
Troubleshooting applications
Observability of AWS resources

✅ 7. What is API in AWS?

API = Application Programming Interface
In AWS, Amazon API Gateway is used to:

Create and manage APIs
Connect frontend with backend services
Secure and scale APIs

💡 Key Takeaway:
Focus on real-time scenarios, CI/CD pipelines, and Kubernetes troubleshooting for DevOps interviews.
